## Sources

Where the data comes from and how the dictionary is derived from it.
{% if external_release %}
The source data is not in this repo: the build gets it as input from the repo that releases the dictionary.
{%- elif source_updates %}
The sources are locked to a version in `sources.lock.json`.
The *Update* workflow checks them weekly, commits newer versions and releases the dictionary if it changed.
{%- else %}
The sources never change and are vendored in `vendored_sources/`.
{%- endif %}

## Installation

Make sure [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) is installed on your system and run

``` bash
uv sync
```

## Usage

``` bash
uv run build.py
```

This creates the dictionary in `out/` (`{{ repo_name }}.zip`, `{{ repo_name }}.index.json` and `{{ repo_name }}.manifest.json`).
Downloaded sources are cached in `tmp/sources/`, the uncompressed dictionary is kept in `tmp/{{ repo_name }}/` for inspection.

## Development

``` bash
uv run ruff check .          # lint
uv run ruff format .         # format
uv run pyright               # type check
uv run pytest                # tests
```

The repo follows the [DaLang dictionary repo standard](https://github.com/dariyooo/dalang-dict-authoring/blob/main/docs/repo-standard.md),
update the shared setup with `uvx copier update --trust`.

## Release
{% if external_release %}
This repo holds the build code only. The dictionary is built and released from another repo, which has the source
data: it checks out this repo, runs the build with the data and publishes the result as a release here.
Installed dictionaries pick up new releases through "Check for updates".
{% else %}

Push a tag with today's date:

``` bash
git tag 2026-11-01 && git push origin 2026-11-01
```

The *Release* workflow runs the checks, builds the dictionary with the tag as revision and publishes it as the GitHub release of the tag.
To redo a release, push the tag again with `git tag -f 2026-11-01 && git push -f origin 2026-11-01`.
Installed dictionaries pick up new releases through "Check for updates".
{% endif %}

